    "['ipv6 address [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:db8:1::1/64', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Cisco `ipv6 address` configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:db8:1::1/64\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper:\\n1. Interface naming follows `ge-x/y/z` format (GigabitEthernet becomes ge)\\n2. You must specify a logical unit (typically 0)\\n3. The address is assigned under the `family inet6` hierarchy\\n4. The command uses `set` prefix for configuration mode\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6 address 2001:db8:1::1/64'}]]": 1,
