ally done globally rather than per interface like Cisco. The equivalent would be enabling IPv6 at the protocol level. If you specifically need interface-level IPv6 enablement in Juniper, it would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces <interface-name> family inet6\\n##\\n\\nFor the exact Cisco \"ipv6 enable\" interface command translation, the second option is more accurate. For your specific configuration (e.g., for GigabitEthernet1/0/0), it would be:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6\\n##', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family inet6'}]]": 1,
