    "['no synchronization', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'no synchronization', 'parent_command': ['set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'family inet6'], 'root': 'set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nno synchronization\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent BGP synchronization behavior is different - Juniper Junos doesn\\'t have the exact same \"no synchronization\" command since BGP synchronization is not enabled by default in Junos (unlike some Cisco IOS versions where it was enabled by default). If you specifically wanted to ensure synchronization is disabled in Junos (though it already is), you would use:\\n##\\nset protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize\\n##\\n\\nHowever, for a direct 1:1 translation of \"no synchronization\" from Cisco to Juniper, the first answer is most accurate since it represents the same state (synchronization disabled).', 'trans_template': 'no synchronization'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize', 'parent_command': ['set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'family inet6'], 'root': 'set routing-options autonomous-system [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nno synchronization\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, the equivalent BGP synchronization behavior is different - Juniper Junos doesn\\'t have the exact same \"no synchronization\" command since BGP synchronization is not enabled by default in Junos (unlike some Cisco IOS versions where it was enabled by default). If you specifically wanted to ensure synchronization is disabled in Junos (though it already is), you would use:\\n##\\nset protocols bgp group <group-name> no-synchronize\\n##\\n\\nHowever, for a direct 1:1 translation of \"no synchronization\" from Cisco to Juniper, the first answer is most accurate since it represents the same state (synchronization disabled).', 'trans_template': 'set protocols bgp group <gro